Preserve Codex permissions across remote resumes

Use Codex 0.154.0 in the isolated test package and wait for the ready
screen before submitting test prompts.

Send the effective bypass setting on the existing pod WebSocket request
and refresh it when a frontend reuses the daemon's cached proxy. Apply
permission defaults when the pod starts its Codex app-server so remote
resumes no longer receive the frontend overrides that Codex rejects.

A running app-server keeps its startup defaults, while saved threads
retain their permissions. Each new connection supplies the setting again
so app-server and pod restarts do not require separate persisted state.
